      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(process): report actual elapsed time for early lane timeouts",
        "body": "Closes #109219\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where operators investigating an early command-lane release would see the configured task budget presented as elapsed time. A lane released after seconds could therefore claim that it had timed out after roughly 48 hours.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe queue now keeps its existing timeout and lane-release policy while formatting each timeout arm with its actual cause and measured duration. Task-budget, progress-idle, abort-grace, and caller-requested release paths remain distinguishable without changing error classification or queue scheduling.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCommand-lane timeout diagnostics now show why the lane was released and separate measured elapsed time from the configured task budget, reducing misleading incident investigation signals. This is observability-only; timeout behavior and defaults are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\nReal production-path harness using the exported command queue and real timers, with a 172,830,000ms task budget and a caller-owned release after 40ms:\n\nBefore (`upstream/main`):\n\n```text\n[diagnostic] lane task error: lane=proof-release durationMs=41 error=\"CommandLaneTaskTimeoutError: Command lane \"proof-release\" task timed out after 172830000ms\"\n{\"elapsedMs\":63,\"name\":\"CommandLaneTaskTimeoutError\",\"message\":\"Command lane \\\"proof-release\\\" task timed out after 172830000ms\"}\n```\n\nAfter:\n\n```text\n[diagnostic] lane task error: lane=proof-release durationMs=42 error=\"CommandLaneTaskTimeoutError: Command lane \"proof-release\" task timed out: lane release requested after 42ms (task budget 172830000ms)\"\n{\"elapsedMs\":63,\"name\":\"CommandLaneTaskTimeoutError\",\"message\":\"Command lane \\\"proof-release\\\" task timed out: lane release requested after 42ms (task budget 172830000ms)\"}\n```\n\nFocused regression coverage exercises task-budget, progress-idle, abort-grace, and release-signal diagnostics:\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/process/command-queue.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  38 passed (38)\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard\n\n$ git diff --check\n# clean\n```\n\nThe final structured pre-commit review reported no accepted/actionable findings and rated the lint-complete patch correct with 0.98 confidence. Broad type/lint and full-suite validation are left to fork PR CI because this linked contributor worktree has no supported Testbox/Crabbox backend.\n\nAI-assisted; implementation and focused proof were reviewed and run manually.\n",
        "branch": "fix/109219-command-lane-timeout-diagnostics",
